sb-swift tls-echo is ready (verified on loopback: matching PSK -> echoOk/exit 0; wrong PSK or unknown identity -> E004/exit 4).

Build (from repo root):
  swift build -c release --package-path Conformance/SwiftHarness

Binary:
  $(swift build -c release --package-path Conformance/SwiftHarness --show-bin-path)/sb-swift
  currently: Conformance/SwiftHarness/.build/out/Products/Release/sb-swift

Server:
  sb-swift tls-echo --role server --listen 127.0.0.1:0 --identity ID --psk-hex <64 hex>
  -> {"event":"listening","port":N,"pskFingerprint":"..."}   then per connection {"event":"tlsEstablished"}
     (failed handshakes print {"code":"E004","event":"error"} and the server keeps running)
Client:
  sb-swift tls-echo --role client --connect 127.0.0.1:N --identity ID --psk-hex <64 hex>
  -> sends "ping\n", expects echo, prints {"event":"echoOk"} exit 0; else {"event":"error","code":"E004",...} exit 4

Parameters: NetworkParameters.serverSession/clientSession (TLS 1.2 only, suite 0xCCAC, no tickets/resumption/renegotiation).
Identity is the UTF-8 bytes of --identity.
